      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors present the clinical history of a 66 year old woman with a previous anterior myocardial infarction and periinfarct ischemia as well as ischemia in another area not related to the scar (in the posterolateral region of the left ventricle) in whom they successfully performed percutaneous coronary angioplasty of the anterior descending and circumflex arteries since the patient was not a candidate for surgical revascularization because of her clinical condition."},
